Hi, all:
	
HISTORY:
	This POTD is porting from DNI R7500 GPL code, comptialble  in our DUT using NAND FLASH structure.



HOW TO USE:
	potd: as "pot run", it is a daemon calculate power on time 
	potval: a server listening utility tool and response POT stauts (NTGR spec have definition but FOXCONN not implement!!)
	stamac: (get/set) [if (active==set)?mac:""], sign up the first STA (wireless)  device (MAC format XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX) diffrent Foxconn (XX-XX-XX-XX-XX), same as "pot mac_record [XX-XX-XX]"   
	ntpstat: (get/set), same as "pot ntp_record", sign up the time status

TROUBLESHOOTING:
	1.in FLASH NAND DUT always store in /misc3/POT, if you are not carefully delete this file, use command "echo -n POTTOP>> /misc3/POT;pot erase".
	2.Foxconn "pot value" and "potd" cannot read the value ?
		Because "pot value" read nvram you might up the "pot run" in system will reload in memory will be work
FUTURE
	1.implement client utility with POT
	2.More comptialbility in our pot 
	3.implement POT erase
	



